{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789247596,"nonce":"Q4P6CeQDg2shu06Pjg7XAaxgUCM=","title":"Housekeeping: split every module over 1k lines into a directory of smaller modules","message":"Thirty-two files in src/ are over 1,000 lines; the largest are runtime/vm.rs, codegen/runtime_fns.rs, codegen/mod.rs, codegen/cranelift_backend.rs, runtime/vm_interp.rs, codegen/aot.rs and runtime/engine.rs, each 4-8k lines.\n\nFollow Ash's layout: a backend is a directory whose mod.rs holds the driver and shared types, with one file per concern -- crates/ash/src/cranelift/{mod,backend,codegen,lower,air}.rs, crates/ash/src/llvm/function/{mod,air_emit,calls,casts,enums,memory,natives,objects}.rs, crates/ash_interp/src/interpreter/{mod,ops,natives,ssa}.rs. Split by what the code is about (calls, objects, memory, OSR, tiering), not by size alone, and keep each piece under about 1k lines where the seams allow.\n\nCandidates and natural seams:\n- codegen/cranelift_backend.rs: compile driver + OSR entries; instruction lowering by family (arith/compare, calls and inline caches, objects and fields, subscripts and typed arrays, SIMD intrinsics); AOT-only lowering (CHA, state machine); the tier hook and cold-loop exits.\n- codegen/llvm_backend.rs (new in e55c484): same families.\n- codegen/runtime_fns.rs: JIT thread state and context; call stubs per arity; allocation helpers; IC dispatch; OSR exit and re-tier; error routing.\n- codegen/mod.rs: the MachInst lowering that predates Cranelift is most of it; the artifact and executable types are a small module of their own.\n- runtime/vm.rs and runtime/vm_interp.rs: GC root scanning and stack ranges; fiber and error routing; the run loop's opcode families; OSR entry/exit; call dispatch.\n- runtime/engine.rs: registration and per-function tables; tier policy and compile requests; install and poll; IC/CHA/inline-body preparation.\n- codegen/aot.rs, codegen/wasm.rs, hatch.rs, capi.rs, parse/parser.rs, mir/builder.rs, runtime/gc.rs: by construct family.\n\nPure moves: no behaviour change, no renames of public items beyond the module path, one commit per directory so blame stays useful. Run the full test suite and the bench set after each.","files":null}]}